Oracles of the vanilla data of each protocol, which tests hold the data of
vNNNN, and what the session sends, to. The binary embeds none of them.

  vNNNN/creative.json  the creative inventory BDS of the protocol sends,
  vNNNN/crafting.json  and its recipes, items by name, as cmd/vanilla-probe
                       -creative and -crafting write them, from the runs of
                       scripts/bedrock-data.sh that ../vNNNN/PROVENANCE
                       records: BDS 1.26.52.3 for 2193, BDS 1.26.61.1 for
                       2225.

  vNNNN/palette.nbt    the block palette of the protocol, as Geyser keeps it
                       (GeyserMC/Geyser, core/src/main/resources/bedrock/,
                       MIT license, below), ungzipped:
                       v2193 block_palette.26_50.nbt of commit
                         50115039af4cd92e50545075d3a13eea6880cf88,
                         sha256 (gzipped)
                         54c9bed0bef30aadc316b21c6e82b5ac407c5c6e351b9d9690aa4e9a49fec912
                       v2225 block_palette.26_60.nbt of commit
                         fd35d5918ae8e8b6c05d91179315fa00413c1f65,
                         sha256 (gzipped)
                         9d0feee0cd2edc1499bd7f7922615caee4dd268b598fca45dc396f4d0bdcdaa3

The files over 100 KiB are stored zstd-compressed, as .zst, and read
through internal/testfixture. TestWriteOracles writes them again:

  go test -run '^TestWriteOracles$' -oracles-from DIR -palettes-from GEYSER .

where DIR holds the vNNNN folders scripts/bedrock-data.sh wrote and GEYSER
the two palettes of Geyser.

